    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.doc\n\n### Description\n\nHi, is there any plan to add syntax highlighting to codeblocks generated by `MiniDoc.afterlines_to_code`?\r\nI think that this can be added without much overhead as a optional parameter, that is\r\n```lua\r\nMiniDoc.afterlines_to_code = function(struct, lang)\r\n  ...\r\n  return '>' .. (lang or '') .. '\\n' .. src .. '\\n<'\r\n```\r\n",
